{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Shechem one.</b> Some say that he alluded to the city of Shechem, for it too belonged to the children of Joseph," "and the sense of \"with my sword and with my bow\" is upon the Name, as David said, \"my shield and the horn of my salvation\" (Psalms 18:3, 2 Samuel 22:3). But the correct interpretation in my eyes is that שכם אחד means \"one portion,\" and it is from the family of על שכמם (Exodus 12:34), ולעבדו שכם אחד (Zephaniah 3:9)," "over your brothers, in addition to your brothers," "and the sense of \"which I took\" — which Israel will take with their sword and with their bow. And he mentioned the Amorite because among the seven nations there is none as mighty as he. Do you not see that after the two great kings of the Amorite were slain, Joshua said, \"to deliver us into the hand of the Amorite\" (Joshua 7:7)? And do not wonder at the word לקחתי, for after HaShem gave it by mouth to Abraham, they consider it as though it is theirs, and likewise it was said to Jacob, \"to you I will give it and to your seed\" (Genesis 13:15):"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {1 "The phrase על משפחת appears elliptical; read literally as \"from the family of\" with the verse citations serving as parallels for the usage of שכם meaning portion."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:20.787708099Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}